2. advisory — brief:90 `[severity: S4]` The same cwd-relative spawn also exists in files this opus runs but does not own. `apps/web/test/w675.test.ts:131-132` is b6's Genuine red at brief:105. `apps/web/test/w467.test.ts:27,31` and `apps/web/test/w300.test.ts:11,18` are reused. None of these is stated as a limit. Replacement, appended to the row: "the reused wrappers `w675.test.ts`, `w467.test.ts` and `w300.test.ts` resolve the served config relative to the caller's cwd and are replayed only from the repo root; that is a limit." [class: web×cwd-relative-test-path] — check: none: a policy row refusing a relative `--config=` with `cwd: process.cwd()` in any `apps/web/test/*.test.ts` spawn.
3. advisory — brief:78 `[severity: S2]` Rows 78–81 name `homeNeeds()`, `homeSummary()` and `assert.deepEqual()` as rejecting functions. With `w503.test.ts` out of `test:policy` (package.json:12), those Node assertions now run in no CI path. Only the served `expect()` checks in `tests-serve/w503.spec.ts` reject in CI. The rows still fail closed through those served checks, but they claim more CI coverage than exists. Replacement for the Rejected-by cell of brief:78–81: "served `expect()` in `tests-serve/w503.spec.ts` (CI, `test:serve`); `homeNeeds()`/`homeSummary()` `assert.deepEqual()` in `w503.test.ts` only on focused replay." [class: web×test-not-in-ci-path] — check: apps/web/tests-serve/w503.spec.ts
4. advisory — brief:115 `[severity: S4]` The claim that b1–b3 "remain mandatory in `test:serve`" holds today: the config has `testDir: "./tests-serve"` with no grep or testIgnore, the titles are at w503.spec.ts:14,29,132, and ci.yml:184-187 runs `test:serve` after the browser install with no `continue-on-error`. But no row pins the claim. A later testIgnore or rename would drop these rows without failing any check. Replacement: append "pinned by the r24 host `served-b123.log` listing all three W-503-b titles under `playwright.serve.config.ts`." [class: web×test-not-in-ci-path] — check: none: a policy row asserting each served W-503-b title is listed by `playwright test --list --config=playwright.serve.config.ts`.

